# Raw source documents — track provenance in data/README.md, not in git
data/raw/*
!data/raw/.gitkeep

# Generated dataset (~8 MB) — COMMITTED DELIBERATELY, not ignored.
#
# It regenerates from seed 26, so ignoring it looks tempting. But generation
# renders text with whatever font the machine provides (Arial on Windows,
# Liberation or DejaVu on Linux and Colab), and glyph outlines differ enough to
# change segmentation. On Colab, thinner strokes split characters in half:
# clean_digital CER went from 6.5% to 63.7% purely from the rendering.
#
# Committing the data makes every machine see identical crops, so the report,
# the notebooks and web/model.json agree everywhere. Regenerate only if you
# intend to change the dataset:
#   python data/generate_dataset.py --docs-per-tier 12 --seed 26 --force

# The trained OCR backend (integration/ocr_backend.npz) is COMMITTED, not
# ignored. Training is not bit-reproducible across BLAS builds, so a retrained
# backend no longer matches web/model.json and the browser parity check fails.

# Benchmark outputs ARE committed (results.json / results.md) — they are the
# evidence behind the report and must be reviewable without running anything.

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

